From 3e8cdb2a1fcf266065c69a1a3cc22a1f10d14c39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude-cpu <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:41:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] SPU: interpret unlifted functions instead of halting
 (spu_interp_call)

A call from lifted SPU code into a function the static lift never saw
(vtable methods built at runtime) ended the whole SPU program with
BRANCH-TO-0. spu_interp_call interprets it from live LS and rejoins
compiled code at the call/return/tail boundaries the lifter uses.
Default on; SPU_INTERP_FALLBACK=0 restores the old path.
Test: runtime/spu/tests gen_test_interp_fallback.py + main.
